      "math_academy_id": "q-275234",
      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ and $b=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$\n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{3}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
